import { FilesystemReaderCopy } from "../model"

pub fn copy -> FilesystemReaderCopy = FilesystemReaderCopy {
  summary: "The write mode for creating a new file. An existing destination causes failure instead of being overwritten.",
  taskTitle: "Protect a report with the same name",
  purpose: "Write original to report.txt, then try writing replacement at the same destination. Receive FileAlreadyExists from the second attempt and read back original to check that the file was preserved.",
  setup: "fs, paths, and effects are names introduced by imports. effect fn report directory: paths.Path -> String defines work in directory that returns explanatory text. with FileSystem names the required service; fails ReportError names ordinary failures. Within do, <- receives a result and _ <- waits without keeping it. fs.CreateNew is the first argument to writeTextUtf8.",
  after: [
    "paths.child adds report.txt to directory and returns Left with a problem or Right with a Path. |> passes values to the next function; effects.fromEither turns the result into work. ReportError’s PathFailure, WriteFailure, and ReadFailure hold original problems, wrapped by effects.mapError. deriving Show enables display through show.",
    "The first writeTextUtf8 receives CreateNew, \"original\", and file, in that order. The second also uses CreateNew, so effects.attempt produces Left error as second. attempt captures ordinary failure as a value. match selects Left or Right; the failed branch calls describe error file to build a description.",
    "fn describe takes error and file and returns a String. error.operation is WriteFile; error.kind is FileAlreadyExists. Rendering error.path and file and comparing them with == produces True. otherPath is Just other when a second path exists or Nothing when absent. This write displays none.",
    "let names immutable values, and the last string in describe’s block is its return value. ${...} inserts values into text, and effects.succeed makes the completed description a successful result. main uses withTemporaryDirectory to supply a workspace and remove it afterward. attempt and match choose the text for println. The final contents: original confirms the preserved content."
  ],
  details: [
    "CreateNew is one of WriteMode’s three choices and takes no arguments. Write fs.CreateNew, not fs.CreateNew (). It checks exclusive creation when the file is opened; an earlier exists check is not a substitute.",
    "Choose Replace when intentionally replacing content, or Append when retaining it and adding to the end. Ignoring CreateNew’s failure and switching to Replace would lose the existing report this example is protecting.",
    "This mode rejects duplicate creation, but does not guarantee that writing a new file cannot fail. Permissions, output, or closing the file can fail too. A partially created new file may remain; distinguish that possibility from protection against overwriting an existing file."
  ],
  comparisonBefore: "Node-based TS can also use writeFile with flag: \"wx\" to fail with EEXIST when the destination exists. There is no need to combine an existence check with a normal overwriting write.",
  comparisonAfter: "Seseragi expresses the choice as fs.CreateNew and reports FileAlreadyExists through FileSystemError.kind. TS can provide the same protection; the difference here is how the mode and failure appear in types."
}
